We aren’t just building a simulation engine anymore. We’re building an engine for experiencing, interpreting, and transforming reality through different lenses.

The world is the stage. The simulation supplies its inhabitants, events, and causal structure. But the lenses determine what we see, what we notice, what we understand, what we feel, and what the experience means to us.

And we can change those lenses independently, combine them, or move fluidly between them.

Pantheon — The Reality Prism

